# API — audience layout

One Nest API, two HTTP audiences: **staff** (PMS) and **public** (web, Phase 2).

| Folder | Role |
|--------|------|
| `src/staff/` | PMS HTTP only — controllers + guards; URLs under `/staff/...` |
| `src/domain/` | Shared services, input DTOs, mappers — **no** controllers, **no** staff/public guards |
| `src/public/` | Web HTTP only — URLs under `/public/...` (scaffold until Phase 2) |
| `src/common/` | Cross-cutting (envelope, pagination base, staff mapper helpers) |

- Staff-only features (auth, admin users) may keep service + controller under `staff/<feature>/`.
- Logic both audiences will need (inventory, later availability / booking core) → `domain/<feature>/`; staff HTTP in `staff/`; public HTTP in `public/` when it exists.
- Never share one controller across staff + public. Never loosen guards on `/staff/*` for the website — add a `public/` controller that calls `domain/`.
- Never ship audience-neutral app paths (`/properties`, `/admins`). `/health` is infra-only.
- Wire types: `Staff*` in `@cabin/api-contract` = staff/PMS shapes. Website gets its own thinner types later — do not treat `Staff*` as the public catalog.

